The only thing I can find about tameness on revival is;
wary_dog:
/*
 * Called during pet revival or pet life-saving.
 * If you killed the pet, it revives wild.
 * If you abused the pet a lot while alive, it revives wild.
 * If you abused the pet at all while alive, it revives untame.
 * If the pet wasn't abused and was very tame, it might revive tame.
 */

So, if you're nice to your pet, it'll come back to fight for you
again. Also, you can always use a scroll of taming. If you haven't
abused it, it has 1-in-tameness chance of going wild (The comment
mentions Pet Semetary, in fact). I guess that would be a 1-in-20
chance normally, since trolls eat.

It seems you can abuse your pet by:
-Kicking it
-Displacing it into a trap (the kind that actually traps them, or a
level teleporter?)
-Trying to untrap it out of a bear trap and failing.
-Hitting it 

(It looks like being hit by spells don't abuse it though)

So, as long as you're not wielding Stormy and are careful when
throwing stuff and getting out of traps, you should be ok. But you
might as well keep a scroll of taming around, and pick up any
artifacts before it revives, just in case.

This is from 5 minutes of looking at the source, and might be
mistaken. Any source-divers care to correct this?

